7. DEFENDER FRONTIER NEW =E2=80=94 OX Cloud / agent runtime defence

OX Security launched OX Cloud on Sep 16; current coverage describes a
CNAPP-style cloud security layer paired with runtime defence for AI agents
accessing cloud data, tools and actions.

*Technical delta:* conventional cloud posture/workload context is being
connected to agent runtime behavior rather than agent security living only
as prompt filtering or MCP scanning.

*Why serious defenders may use it:* agents increasingly inherit cloud
identities and operate across resources that existing CNAPP products
already understand. Runtime agent controls attached to that graph can
potentially reason over both cloud exposure and agent action.

*Key questions for recheck:* Is enforcement actually inline? What event
schema captures agent/tool actions? Does it distinguish agent principal
from human/service principal? Does it inspect hostile tool output? Is there
an open telemetry/API path we can test?

*Decision:* WATCH. Promote to BUILD PROBE comparison only after primary
technical docs expose enforcement architecture.
